# Webisters Framework

PHP 8.2+ MVC framework. Entry class is `App` (project root `App.php`), extends `Framework\MVC\App`.

## Directory layout

- `App.php` - project App class
- `boot/` - `init.php`, `constants.php`, `helpers.php`, `app.php`, `routes.php`
- `app/Controllers/` - `App\Controllers\*`, extend `Framework\MVC\Controller`
- `app/Models/` - `App\Models\*`, extend `Framework\MVC\Model`
- `app/Views/` - PHP view templates
- `config/` - one PHP file per service, returns `['default' => [...]]`
- `public/index.php` - HTTP entry point
- `storage/` - writable runtime files

## Service container

```php
App::database()    App::router()     App::request()    App::response()
App::session()     App::cache()      App::view()        App::logger()
App::mailer()      App::validation() App::language()   App::console()
App::migrator()    App::antiCsrf()
```

All accept optional `$instance = 'default'`.

## Routing

```php
// boot/routes.php
App::router()->serve(null, static function (RouteCollection $routes) : void {
    $routes->namespace('App\Controllers', [
        $routes->get('/', 'Home::index', 'home.index'),
        $routes->post('/users', 'Users::store', 'users.store'),
    ]);
    $routes->notFound(static fn () => respond_not_found());
});
```

## Conventions

- All PHP files: `<?php declare(strict_types=1);`
- Config files return `['default' => [...]]`; env values via `env('key', 'default')`
- Do not modify `vendor/` or the license header comment block in PHP files

## Commands

```bash
php webisters start                  # dev server port 8000
php webisters route:list             # list routes
php webisters make:controller <Name>
php webisters make:model <Name>
php webisters make:view <path/name>
php webisters migrate:up
vendor/bin/phpunit
vendor/bin/php-cs-fixer fix
```
